    "result_text": "The acceptance suite is the only test suite, and it's fully green. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the registration-date rule for `POST /api/owners` so that when no registration date is supplied it defaults to the server's current date, and `registrationDate` is returned in ISO `YYYY-MM-DD` format.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added an optional `registrationDate` property (`type: string`, `format: date`) to the `OwnerFields` schema. The `date` format makes the generated `OwnerFieldsDto`/`OwnerDto` use `LocalDate`, which Jackson serializes as ISO `YYYY-MM-DD`. Being on `OwnerFields`, it is both accepted on create and returned by `GET`.\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 Added a `registrationDate` (`LocalDate`) field mapped to a `registration_date` column, plus getter/setter. MapStruct maps it automatically in both directions.\n\n3. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 When the mapped owner has no `registrationDate`, it's set to `LocalDate.now()`; a supplied date is preserved.\n\n4. **Schema SQL** (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `postgres`, `mysql`) \u2014 Added a nullable `registration_date DATE` column to the `owners` table so the value round-trips through persistence. (Tests run on hsqldb; the others are kept consistent.)\n\nResults: the two new `Cp07Tests` pass, and the full suite is green \u2014 `Tests run: 14, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`, BUILD SUCCESS.",
